WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.230 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  police used water cannon on these  protesters in the southern city of  siruvananthapuram on saturday  they were among thousands of people  around the country  who heeded farmers calls to join their  movement  many stopped traffic by sitting on roads  and at toll collection centers in the  states of jammu rajasthan haryana  punjab and telangana they said they  wanted to show their solidarity with  those who've been blocking the highways  around delhi  for more than two months  there are at least 80 places in punjab  where farmers groups are protesting and  blocking roads against narendra modi's  government and the farm laws  to force them to roll them back there is  a blockade here at the golden gate too  [Music]  fifty thousand police and paramilitary  personnel have been deployed in  and around the capital new delhi police  say they're taking extra precautions  since the outbreaks of violence between  police and protesters on  india's republic day january 26th  since republic day police have erected  many rows of barricades outside the  three major protest sites on delhi's  outskirts making them  very difficult to access water  electricity and internet services have  been  intermittently cut off at the sites  where hundreds of thousands of people  are camping out  the un's human rights office has asked  the indian government and protesters to  exercise maximum restraint  but also said the right to peaceful  assembly and expression should be  protected both  offline and online  the government has arrested more than  120 people in connection with the recent  violence  and charged farm union leaders with  writing and sedition  it's also had hundreds of twitter  accounts suspended  farmers say the government is treating  them like criminals  farmers are not that aggressive that  barbed wire has to be put up  the government shouldn't have done this  farmers are not from some foreign  country  they are people of the same country as  modi even a child doesn't behave the way  modi does  and he's a senior citizen they shouldn't  be resorting to such measures to stop  farmers  this is absolutely wrong farmers say  they are undeterred by the government's  crackdown  and will continue their protests until  the agriculture laws are repealed  elizabeth puranam al-jazeera gazipur  uttar pradesh

